CON-20: give a swale the pervious area's infiltration rate, not a diluted one

findNativeInfil() set the native soil infiltration rate that a vegetative
swale uses (when the subcatchment does not use Green-Ampt) to the
infiltration volume of the non-LID pervious subarea divided by the whole
non-LID area. That is the pervious area's rate times its fraction of the
subcatchment, so a swale in a 90 % impervious subcatchment infiltrated at
a tenth of the soil's rate. Divide by the pervious subarea's area instead,
which gives the rate "computed for the pervious area of the subcatchment"
that the reference manual specifies.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CON-20_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/lid.c b/src/legacy/engine/lid.c
index e2ac45a..a812a7c 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/lid.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/lid.c
@@ -1752,7 +1752,8 @@ void findNativeInfil(int j, double tStep)
     nonLidArea = Subcatch[j].area - Subcatch[j].lidArea;
     if ( nonLidArea > 0.0 && Subcatch[j].fracImperv < 1.0 )
     {
-        NativeInfil = Vinfil / nonLidArea / tStep;
+        NativeInfil = Vinfil / (nonLidArea * Subcatch[j].subArea[PERV].fArea) /
+                      tStep;
     }
 
     //... otherwise find infil. rate for the subcatchment's rainfall + runon
